## Why This Is Asked

Tests a constrained subsequence DP with gap bounds and reconstruction, a common real-world scheduling/selection pattern.

## Key Concepts

- DP on sequences with restricted gaps
- State dp[i][t] and transition over a window [i-U, i-L]
- Path reconstruction with parent pointers

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxSumWithGaps(A, k, L, U){
  const n = A.length, NEG = -1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({length: k+1}, ()=> Array(n).fill(NEG));
  const par = Array.from({length: k+1}, ()=> Array(n).fill(-1));
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++) dp[1][i] = A[i];
  for(let t=2;t<=k;t++){
    for(let i=0;i<n;i++){
      let best = NEG, bestj = -1;
      for(let j=i-U;j<=i-L;j++){
        if(j>=0 && dp[t-1][j] > best){ best = dp[t-1][j]; bestj = j; }
      }
      if(bestj!=-1){ dp[t][i] = A[i] + best; par[t][i] = bestj; }
    }
  }
  let end = -1, best = NEG;
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++) if(dp[k][i] > best){ best = dp[k][i]; end = i; }
  const indices = [];
  let cur = end;
  for(let t=k; t>=1; t--){ indices.push(cur); cur = par[t][cur]; }
  indices.reverse();
  return {best, indices};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a practical DP over partitions with a non-trivial subproblem (distinct counts) and reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- DP over contiguous partitions
- Precomputation of distinct counts for all subarrays
- Backpointers for block reconstruction

## Code Example
```javascript
// Distinct counts precomputation
for (let l = 0; l < n; l++) {
  const freq = new Map();
  let dist = 0;
  for (let r = l; r < n; r++) {
    const x = logs[r];
    if ((freq.get(x) || 0) === 0) dist++;
    freq.set(x, (freq.get(x) || 0) + 1);
    distinctCount[l][r] = dist;
  }
}

// DP
for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) dp[i][1] = distinctCount[0][i-1];
for (let t = 2; t <= k; t++) {
  for (let i = t; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let j = t-1; j < i; j++) {
      const val = dp[j][t-1] + distinctCount[j][i-1];
      if (val > dp[i][t]) { dp[i][t] = val; par[i][t] = j; }
    }
  }
}
```

